# .github/versions.env: tools the workflows put on the runner themselves, and the public fallbacks of the company base
# images, pinned (ADR-0021, ADR-0033). One line each, so a bump is a one-line change. Read by .github/actions/setup-yq
# through scripts/ci/setup-yq.sh, by .github/actions/setup-build-env and by scripts/ci/public-base-smoke.sh. A
# `# renovate:` hint names the datasource and package of the KEY=value line below it, like test-infra/kind/versions.env.
# Comments stay on lines of their own; values are plain (no quotes, no spaces).

# mikefarah yq v4: the YAML processor of the workflows, of pool-deploy.sh and of the script tests (ADR-0030) — not
# the Python wrapper of the same name. The runner gets exactly this version; GitHub-hosted runners carry another v4,
# which is shadowed. Downloaded from the GitHub release, or from the generic remote named by the repository variable
# YQ_DOWNLOAD_BASE behind JFrog, and checked against the SHA-256 the release publishes.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=mikefarah/yq
YQ_VERSION=v4.54.1

# The public fallbacks of the company base images (ADR-0033). setup-build-env uses one when <registry>/base/jre21 or
# <registry>/base/ci-build is not published and docker/base/<name>/Dockerfile does not exist: a repository built from
# this one, before its base images exist. The JRE is the base of the app images; the JDK runs the integration tests
# (it-runner). Full references, as Podman needs; Renovate reads the tag after the last ':'. The tags float within
# Java 21, the build's version (ADR-0007): a new major is a decision, so Renovate waits for approval.
# renovate: datasource=docker depName=docker.io/library/eclipse-temurin
BASE_IMAGE_FALLBACK=docker.io/library/eclipse-temurin:21-jre
# renovate: datasource=docker depName=docker.io/library/eclipse-temurin
CI_BUILD_IMAGE_FALLBACK=docker.io/library/eclipse-temurin:21-jdk
